rules.d/ — project rules, concatenated into the system prompt

Every *.md here is injected verbatim, in alphabetical order, on every turn.
Numeric prefixes give that order a meaning: 10-, 20-, 30-.

Because they are always present, they cost context on every request. Keep
them short, factual and about THIS tree: conventions a reader could not infer
from the code, build invariants, the shape of the repository. Anything a
retrieval could find belongs in a skill or a corpus instead.

corpora/<name>.md is read only when that corpus is the session's, which is
where per-project rules go.

This directory ships with no rules. They describe a particular organisation's
code and conventions, so they are yours to write and yours to keep -- outside
the repository, or in your own downstream.
